{"source_id":"arXiv:math/0508143","title":"\\LargeVerma modules for Yangians","abstract":"We study the Verma modules M(mu(u)) over the Yangian Y(a) associated with a simple Lie algebra a. We give necessary and sufficient conditions for irreducibility of M(mu(u)). Moreover, regarding the simple quotient L(mu(u)) of M(mu(u)) as an a-module, we give necessary and sufficient conditions for finite-dimensionality of the weight subspaces of L(mu(u)).","authors":["Y. Billig","V. Futorny","A. Molev"],"year":"2005","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0508143","doi":"10.48550/arXiv.math/0508143","cluster":"quantum_algebra","cards":[{"card_id":"ma-c-e841c842fca1a440a8ff","label":"Abstract","kind":"abstract","line":157,"snippet":"We study the Verma modules $M(\\mu(u))$ over the Yangian $\\Y(\\agot)$ associated with a simple Lie algebra $\\agot$. We give necessary and sufficient conditions for irreducibility of $M(\\mu(u))$. …"},{"card_id":"ma-c-df7d88623f6b1f787455","label":"Equation mui","kind":"equation","line":210,"snippet":"\\mu_i(u)=1+\\mu_i^{(0)}u^{-1}+\\mu_i^{(1)}u^{-2}+\\cdots, \\mu_i^{(r)}\\in\\CC,"},{"card_id":"ma-c-d50593c910baa77c274e","label":"Equation ef","kind":"equation","line":299,"snippet":"[h_i^{(r)},h_j^{(s)}]=0, [e_i^{(r)},f_j^{(s)}]=\\delta_{ij}h_i^{(r+s)}, [h_i^{(0)},e_j^{(s)}]=d_i\\tss a_{ij}e_j^{(s)}, [h_i^{(0)},f_j^{(s)}]=-d_i\\tss a_{ij}f_j^{(s)},\\non [h_i^{(r+1)},e_j^{(s)}] …"},{"card_id":"ma-c-63c5274434fb74ae6723","label":"Equation ordmon","kind":"equation","line":407,"snippet":"f_{\\al^{(1)}}^{(r_1)}\\cdots f_{\\al^{(l)}}^{(r_l)}\\ts 1_{\\mu}, l\\geqslant 0, r_i\\geqslant 0, \\al^{(i)}\\in\\Delta^+"},{"card_id":"ma-c-4c8feba76748cc2b5373","label":"Equation weidec","kind":"equation","line":413,"snippet":"M(\\mu(u))=\\underset{\\eta}{\\oplus}\\ts M(\\mu(u))_{\\eta},"},{"card_id":"ma-c-7785168f190d68949b79","label":"Equation weta","kind":"equation","line":425,"snippet":"\\eta=\\mu^{(0)}-k_1\\al_1-\\cdots-k_n\\al_n,"},{"card_id":"ma-c-afef1ba499d8cc03ce